1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,449
The Cyberia wallet. Two assets in it,
and nothing else.

2
00:00:03,569 --> 00:00:11,179
Liquidity is one level down.

3
00:00:11,299 --> 00:00:14,980
A pool is two assets held together at
one price.

4
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:20,470
CYBER on one side.

5
00:00:20,590 --> 00:00:24,643
USDC on the other — a dollar on this
chain.

6
00:00:24,763 --> 00:00:30,052
You type one amount.

7
00:00:30,172 --> 00:00:33,850
The pool’s own price fills the other.
Arriving at any other ratio would be
partly handed back.

8
00:00:33,970 --> 00:00:38,051
That is 0.0724% of the pool —
0.000000035962 LP.

9
00:00:38,171 --> 00:00:41,652
Both sides get a floor, and both are
written into the transaction.

10
00:00:41,772 --> 00:00:48,179
Hold to sign. A tap is something a thumb
does by accident.

11
00:00:48,299 --> 00:00:55,154
Broadcast is not settlement, so the
wallet waits for the block before it
reads the position back.

12
00:00:55,274 --> 00:01:00,454
The LP token is the position. It earns
the pool’s trading fees on its own.

13
00:01:00,574 --> 00:01:07,851
Staked in the farm, it earns the chain’s
emission as well.

14
00:01:07,971 --> 00:01:15,156
The farm lists every pool, and what this
account holds in them.

15
00:01:15,276 --> 00:01:18,859
All of it.

16
00:01:18,979 --> 00:01:27,283
The farm cannot move the LP yet, so an
allowance is signed first — for exactly
this amount.

17
00:01:27,403 --> 00:01:35,405
Two transactions: the allowance, then
the stake.

18
00:01:35,525 --> 00:01:38,405
And now it pays.

19
00:01:38,525 --> 00:01:50,519
The reward moves every block — the
chain’s own arithmetic, carried forward
from the last read rather than animated.

20
00:01:50,639 --> 00:02:04,578
Claiming takes what has accrued and
leaves the stake where it is.

21
00:02:04,698 --> 00:02:09,864
Claimed, and already accruing again.
